---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import GrievancePending from '../components/GrievancePending.astro';
import { business, fullAddress } from '../config/site';
---
<Legal title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${business.legalName} (${business.brand}) collects, uses and protects personal data.`}>
  <p>This policy explains how <strong>{business.legalName}</strong> ("{business.brand}", "we"), {fullAddress.join(', ')}, processes personal data when you use curiosta.com, request a quotation or buy from us. We act as the Data Fiduciary under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and follow the Information Technology Act, 2000 and rules made under it.</p>

  <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Enquiries and quotations:</strong> name, organisation, email, phone, the product or requirement you describe and any files you send.</li>
    <li><strong>Orders:</strong> billing and shipping address, GSTIN (if provided), order and invoice details.</li>
    <li><strong>Payments:</strong> when online payment is available, payments are processed by Razorpay. We receive the payment status, transaction reference and limited details such as the payment method type. We never receive or store full card numbers, CVV, UPI PIN or netbanking passwords.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> our hosting provider keeps standard server and CDN logs (IP address, browser, pages requested, time) for security and troubleshooting. This website does not use advertising or analytics cookies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to enquiries and prepare quotations (based on your request and consent).</li>
    <li>To process orders, payments, delivery, invoicing, warranty and support (to perform our contract with you).</li>
    <li>To meet legal obligations, including GST and accounting record-keeping.</li>
    <li>To keep the website and our systems secure.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal data and we do not send marketing messages without your consent.</p>

  <h2>3. Who we share it with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Payment processing: Razorpay Software Private Limited.</li>
    <li>Delivery: courier and logistics partners (name, address, phone).</li>
    <li>Hosting, email and IT providers that process data on our behalf (for example Amazon Web Services).</li>
    <li>Our accountants and tax advisers, and government authorities where required by law.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>Enquiry data is kept for up to 3 years after our last contact unless it becomes part of an order. Order and invoice records are kept for as long as GST and other laws require (currently at least 72 months from the due date of the annual return for the relevant year). Server logs are kept for a short period for security purposes.</p>

  <h2>5. Security</h2>
  <p>We use reasonable security safeguards, including encrypted connections (HTTPS), access controls and reputable service providers. No system is perfectly secure; we will notify affected users and authorities of a personal data breach as the law requires.</p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask to access, correct, update or erase your personal data, withdraw consent (this does not affect processing already done or data we must keep by law), and nominate another person to exercise your rights. Email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>. We will respond within a reasonable time and in any case as required by law.</p>

  <h2>7. Children</h2>
  <p>Our products and website are intended for institutions, businesses and adults. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.</p>

  <h2>8. Grievance Officer</h2>
  <p>{business.grievance.name}, {business.grievance.designation} <GrievancePending /><br />{business.legalName}, {fullAddress.join(', ')}<br />Email: <a href={`mailto:${business.grievance.email}`}>{business.grievance.email}</a> · Phone: {business.grievance.phoneDisplay}</p>
  <p>If you are not satisfied with our response, you may approach the Data Protection Board of India once it is available to receive complaints. See also <a href="/grievance-redressal/">Grievance Redressal</a>.</p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>We will post any changes to this policy on this page with a new effective date.</p>
</Legal>
